---
title: Rhubarb Torte
author: Mary Arntson
category: Desserts
cook time: 50 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@flour{1%cup}
@powdered sugar{5%Tbsp}
@butter{0.5%cup}
@well-beaten eggs{2}
@sugar{1.5%cups}
@flour{0.25%cup}
@salt{3/4%tsp}
@finely cut rhubarb{2%cups}
@whipped cream

**Crust:**
Mix flour, powdered sugar, and butter. Press into ungreased 7x11 pan and bake at 350 degrees for 15 minutes.

**Topping:**
Mix eggs, sugar, flour, salt, and rhubarb. Spoon into crust. Bake at 350 degrees for 35 minutes. Serve warm with whipped cream.
